# Infra and state locality

Prefer self-contained, per-repo solutions over machine-global or shared state.

When designing infra (test concurrency, locks, caches, coordination), don't
introduce folders or state outside the repo or shared across clones. Cap
resources per-repo with a static knob.

Clones are already independent, so cross-repo parallelism is free; favor a small
per-repo cap over a shared coordinator. Hence simulator concurrency is the
per-repo `SRB_SIM_MAX` knob (see `AGENTS.md > Build and test`), not a machine-wide
semaphore in a shared cache directory.
